<div id="algorithm2.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.15.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">13</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\_status\leftarrow\textnormal{{FixbyLLM(}}\textnormal{\emph{test\_case, status, out}}\textnormal{{)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em">FixbyLLM(</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">test_case, status, out</em></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em">)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\_status\leftarrow\textnormal{{FixbyLLM(}}\textnormal{\emph{test\_case, status, out}}\textnormal{{)}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.4.15.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.16" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.16.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">14</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.16.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">if</span><span id="algorithm2.4.16.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><em id="algorithm2.4.16.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;"><math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\_status\ ==\textup{{False}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.738em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif">False</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\_status\ ==\textup{{False}}</annotation></semantics></math></em><span id="algorithm2.4.16.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.16.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.17.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.17.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.17.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.17.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">15</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.17.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">continue</span><span id="algorithm2.4.17.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.18.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.18.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">16</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="score\leftarrow\textnormal{{Priority(}}\textnormal{\emph{test\_case}}\textnormal{{)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em">Priority(</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathsize="0.900em"><em class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">test_case</em></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathsize="0.900em">)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">score\leftarrow\textnormal{{Priority(}}\textnormal{\emph{test\_case}}\textnormal{{)}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.4.18.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.19.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">   </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm2.4.19.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">  </span>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">17</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\leftarrow T\cup\{(test\_case,score)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">e</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\leftarrow T\cup\{(test\_case,score)\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm2.4.19.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">18</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="algorithm2.4.20.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><em id="algorithm2.4.20.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;">T</em><span id="algorithm2.4.20.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; </span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.15690v1/test_case_synthesis.svg" id="S3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/353;" width="476" height="353"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Prompt template for test case synthesis.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fuzzing Executor.</span>
Then, MirrorFuzz selects test cases from the test case pool, applies mutation operations, and executes them to detect potential bugs in DL frameworks.
It identifies bugs by monitoring crashes within the framework.
Furthermore, for newly discovered bugs during fuzz testing, MirrorFuzz updates its bug records to identify more potential shared bugs across APIs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For test case selection, we rank each synthesized test case <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> for API <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> using the following formula:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Priority}(T)=G\cdot(U-C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Priority</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Priority}(T)=G\cdot(U-C)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> represents a synthesized test case, and <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Priority}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Priority</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Priority}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies its ranking score.
The binary flag <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that the generated code includes the API <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, preventing the hallucination issue in LLMs that may generate invalid test cases <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">62</a>]</cite>.
<math id="S3.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> represents the number of unique APIs covered by the test case, aiming to explore diverse API combinations.
<math id="S3.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> represents execution time, which helps prevent long-running test cases from consuming excessive resources.
We select the top 10 test cases with the highest priority scores for subsequent mutation operations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">For the mutation strategy, we randomly select parameters of the API under test and apply three types of mutation operators until the desired number of test cases is generated.
These operators include:
1) boundary value mutation, which randomly inserts boundary values (e.g,. NaN, negative values, extreme numerical values) into the input data;
2) type mutation, which randomly changes the data types of parameters, such as converting <span id="S3.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tf.int32</span> to <span id="S3.SS3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tf.float16</span>; and 3) shape and dimension mutation, which modifies input shapes and sizes, such as reshaping tensors.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For test oracle, we detect bugs by monitoring framework crashes, such as program aborts, segmentation faults, and floating-point exceptions.
Additionally, we observe that certain internal errors do not result in crashes but instead cause the framework to halt, often accompanied by messages such as, “Please report this bug to the relevant platform/organization.”
Therefore, we include these cases in our monitoring process to ensure they are properly recorded and reported.
Since Jittor <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> integrates an operator compiler and tuner, it compiles the entire framework and meta-operators just-in-time.
As a result, we also detect bugs where Jittor encounters compilation failures or internal failures.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">EVALUATION</span></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Implementation</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement MirrorFuzz in Python and select commonly used DL Frameworks, including PyTorch (v2.4.1) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, TensorFlow (2.17.0) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, OneFlow (v0.9) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, and Jittor (v1.3.9.5) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, all of which have been previously studied in DL framework testing research <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.
It utilizes the bs4 library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite> to parse the API documentation of DL frameworks, supporting the API information needs of its three modules.
The buggy API recognition module is developed using the requests library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite> to scrape GitHub issues.
The similar API matching module is implemented based on M3-embedding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>, which is employed to obtain semantic embeddings for API pairs.
We set <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> to 0.35, prioritizing semantic similarity to address the challenges of cross-framework matching.
We then retain the Top-6 similar APIs.
For the LLM, we utilize Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct-AWQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite> for test case synthesis.
Qwen2.5-Coder represents the latest series of code-specific Qwen LLMs, offering significant improvements in code generation, code reasoning, and code fixing.
We obtain the model files from Hugging Face <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite> and deploy them locally.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Setup</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline Selection.</span>
Our approach is an API-level fuzzer, so we focus on state-of-the-art API-level fuzzers, including TENSORSCOPE<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, TitanFuzz<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>, Orion<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite>, FuzzGPT<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, and Future<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite>.
To gain a comprehensive understanding, we also consider model-level fuzzers such as MoCo<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>.
Among these, FuzzGPT and Future are promised to be open-source. However, as of the completion of our work, their code is still not publicly available.
Therefore, we choose TENSORSCOPE, TitanFuzz, Orion, and MoCo as our baselines.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DL Framework.</span>
Since some baselines do not support OneFlow and Jittor, we mainly conduct evaluations on TensorFlow and PyTorch.
Except for the DL Framework versions implemented in MirrorFuzz, we also conduct bug detection for each baseline on PyTorch (v1.31.1) and TensorFlow (2.10.0) to ensure a fair comparison, as these versions are the same as or closest to those used by most baselines, minimizing version differences.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Large Language Models.</span>
To comprehensively evaluate the performance of MirrorFuzz in synthesizing shared bugs using LLMs, we selected Qwen2.5-coder<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">47</a>]</cite>, CodeGemma<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>]</cite>, and CodeLlama<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>, deploying them in a local environment.
The specifications of the LLMs used in our evaluation are listed in Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ IV-B Experimental Setup ‣ IV EVALUATION ‣ MirrorFuzz: Leveraging LLM and Shared Bugs for Deep Learning Framework APIs Fuzzing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>.</p>
</div>
